<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Showers seen for parts of Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Showers seen for parts of Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department on Thursday forecast occasional showers in the Central, Sabaragamuwa, Western and Southern provinces for Thursday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement there would be fairly strong westerly winds over the western slope of the Central hills.</p>
<p>The department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Thursday morning:</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Canyon		   80.5</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    54.5</p>
<p>    Kotmale		  56.0</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 94.5</p>
<p>    Moussakele	     34.5</p>
<p>    Norton		   83.0</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0.5</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   5.3</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
